OL,3,CMeeting to be held on future of
OL,4,C'statistically dangerous' A69
OL,6,FCumberland Councillor Roger Dobson has
OL,7,Fconvened a meeting on the stretch of
OL,8,Fthe A69 between Brampton and M6
OL,9,FJunction 43, which he describes as a
OL,10,F"statistically dangerous corridor".
OL,12,FHe said: "The A69 is not simply a
OL,13,Ftransport corridor ` it is a barrier
OL,14,Fto normal community life. It
OL,15,Fsuppresses walking, cycling and public
OL,16,Ftransport use. Residents cross it
OL,17,Fdaily to reach schools, shops, medical
OL,18,Fservices and community facilities.
OL,20,F"The danger is constant, predictable
OL,21,Fand unacceptable."
OL,1,W{$~k4{$k4~sjw=                 G2/7
OL,2,W/.!+.!/*%/.!+,*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BBorder NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,326,320,120,260,000,100
PN,32503
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F325A1785669497
OL,3,CMeeting to be held on future of
OL,4,C'statistically dangerous' A69
OL,6,FSenior representatives from National
OL,7,FHighways, Cumberland Council, Julie
OL,8,FMinns MP, and candidates for next
OL,9,FMay's Cumbria Mayoral election have
OL,10,Fbeen invited to attend the meeting,
OL,11,Fwhich will take place in Warwick
OL,12,FBridge on Wednesday 29 July.
OL,14,FWhat's the solution?
OL,16,FCllr Dobson is calling for the road to
OL,17,Fbe 'de-trunked', which would make the
OL,18,FA69 the responsibility of the local
OL,19,Fauthority, rather than National
OL,20,FHighways.
OL,1,W{$~k4{$k4~sjw=                 G3/7
OL,2,W/.!+.!/*%/.!+,*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
